{"id": "clm:a7afe97e1485a8e5f0372aa64a2ab11181ab10bf89b0740287cee62ae87c9f06", "type": "statement", "text": "For classic hub-and-spoke networks, Microsoft recommends hub placement when several applications or on-premises clients share private endpoints; an endpoint used by one application can live in its spoke. Apply this general placement guidance to Atlas as an architectural inference. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/security-private-endpoint.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Hub-and-Spoke Atlas Networking"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/architecture/networking/guide/private-link-hub-spoke-network"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:e3680c5008b3f183560e1f34df5d82321c8b997f9c27e438f231d1642547cf2e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:6ec20238313b220d3643cff0efe4e5159e231be933d217e11309a4426750c324", "ev:dc193be66b214d6b0ec69c94cba7f4d62930b989b87d7e043abbe8471f77d5f2"]}
{"id": "clm:76a5722bbb0e62949661c9091bdbc0dfafcd4b9fbea1e155f54cea5d6333101f", "type": "statement", "text": "For centralized inspection, Microsoft recommends a dedicated hub endpoint subnet with explicit NVA routing and SNAT configuration. Endpoint /32 routes propagate across configured peering, so check effective routes when validating the intended inspection path. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/architecture/networking/guide/private-link-hub-spoke-network", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Hub-and-Spoke Atlas Networking"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:e3680c5008b3f183560e1f34df5d82321c8b997f9c27e438f231d1642547cf2e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:205791e545cdc7ddc79d5436a94987d5f735a8495c42f8b7c416298c91c4eda8", "ev:d3b993061f02601870c048823f4f19efaf815b1c4f779e298065bc55872b2b0e"]}
{"id": "clm:dccc09fd0a9344d6dd3e708fdc3e5b66288d5309a5f9e4c6fe3af49b427dba16", "type": "statement", "text": "OneUptime's March 31, 2026 comparison table labels private-endpoint transitive routing unsupported. MongoDB explicitly documents access from peered Azure VNets and ExpressRoute-connected networks, so that table should not rule out a shared Atlas endpoint topology. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://oneuptime.com/blog/post/2026-03-31-mongodb-atlas-private-endpoint/view", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Hub-and-Spoke Atlas Networking"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/security-private-endpoint.md", "https://www.mongodb.com/company/blog/product-release-announcements/announcing-azure-private-link-integration-for-mongo-db-atlas"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:e3680c5008b3f183560e1f34df5d82321c8b997f9c27e438f231d1642547cf2e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:45f380edc5aed9d668c9f99de65bef2503e707d7a173e61073f204b1d13cb759", "ev:4883b04f32328c1c496e5e3c0bbf1d59d2108d2f3f7e78ffda36dbfa3ced21f5", "ev:6ec20238313b220d3643cff0efe4e5159e231be933d217e11309a4426750c324"]}
{"id": "clm:dc894eccaafa4ceb0b7cf13c80ccd9f0aa632932eefaa05cb854dc0a606566b8", "type": "statement", "text": "Atlas implements Azure Private Link with a private endpoint in the customer network and a load-balanced service in the Atlas VNet. Connections originate from the customer side; Atlas cannot initiate connections back through that endpoint. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/security-private-endpoint.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Hub-and-Spoke Atlas Networking"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/security-vpc-peering.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:e3680c5008b3f183560e1f34df5d82321c8b997f9c27e438f231d1642547cf2e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:6ec20238313b220d3643cff0efe4e5159e231be933d217e11309a4426750c324"]}
{"id": "clm:20a4db6b8a95dc08e85867ed76bd84f0118092a534e52936caa80bd8c6120e03", "type": "statement", "text": "Atlas Private Link connections are one-way: Atlas cannot initiate connections back into customer VNets. This narrows the network trust boundary compared with VNet peering. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/security-private-endpoint.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Hub-and-Spoke Atlas Networking"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/company/blog/product-release-announcements/announcing-azure-private-link-integration-for-mongo-db-atlas", "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/security-vpc-peering/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:e3680c5008b3f183560e1f34df5d82321c8b997f9c27e438f231d1642547cf2e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:6ec20238313b220d3643cff0efe4e5159e231be933d217e11309a4426750c324", "ev:936011f1d7d0a178fc367da07bcb79817f4f992c1d5099ce2f7cde9845d9d236"]}
{"id": "clm:bb9732c080376220f42025079c905d56f45d96566629fc1c56d97a05296df2e4", "type": "statement", "text": "Ordinary Azure VNet peering is nontransitive. Peering an application spoke to a hub and the hub to an Atlas VNet does not alone provide an application-to-Atlas path; additional routing or direct connectivity is required. This limitation differs from accessing an endpoint located inside the directly peered hub. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/architecture/networking/architecture/hub-spoke", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Hub-and-Spoke Atlas Networking"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/security-private-endpoint.md", "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/security-vpc-peering.md", "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/architecture/reference-architectures/hybrid-networking/virtual-network-peering"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:e3680c5008b3f183560e1f34df5d82321c8b997f9c27e438f231d1642547cf2e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:38aebd940e8856ba88aa47aa555c39d44ef57c314e84e5098701c29307261c4e", "ev:6ec20238313b220d3643cff0efe4e5159e231be933d217e11309a4426750c324", "ev:f812f6d3580e6adee76c53ffdd4281ba11167c50c0a371a57c9c3ce82e0c3ee8"]}
{"id": "clm:028bf88ff3fc8d8c8fadfbd1b83b600c5550148756c40689596950b8e0ad355c", "type": "statement", "text": "Azure Private Link lets an application in a VNet peered to the endpoint's VNet reach Atlas through that private endpoint. In a traditional hub-and-spoke design, placing the endpoint in the hub therefore allows directly peered spokes to share Atlas access; this placement is an architectural inference from the documented reachability. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/security-private-endpoint.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Hub-and-Spoke Atlas Networking"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/company/blog/product-release-announcements/announcing-azure-private-link-integration-for-mongo-db-atlas", "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/architecture/networking/guide/private-link-hub-spoke-network"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:e3680c5008b3f183560e1f34df5d82321c8b997f9c27e438f231d1642547cf2e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:569b2124a836276dca149d34476faec0cfa3b070e1c3edb42ba28dd14098834d", "ev:6ec20238313b220d3643cff0efe4e5159e231be933d217e11309a4426750c324"]}
{"id": "clm:e172fa1948137cfdb55f764703f8d93cf077e9abd41f3196e6f39dddae4ed2df", "type": "statement", "text": "An on-premises data center connected by ExpressRoute to the private-endpoint VNet can reach Atlas through the endpoint without adding public IP addresses to the Atlas IP access list. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/security-private-endpoint.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Hub-and-Spoke Atlas Networking"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/company/blog/product-release-announcements/announcing-azure-private-link-integration-for-mongo-db-atlas"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:e3680c5008b3f183560e1f34df5d82321c8b997f9c27e438f231d1642547cf2e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:6ec20238313b220d3643cff0efe4e5159e231be933d217e11309a4426750c324"]}
{"id": "clm:e7446463156ba98a46284d0d3673d4dfda11da0490762f4e3680ff2d2e2321f3", "type": "statement", "text": "Azure Virtual WAN does not allow private endpoints inside its virtual or secured hub; deploy them in connected spoke VNets. (low confidence) (verified as of 2025-07-23)", "source_url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/architecture/networking/guide/private-link-hub-spoke-network", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Hub-and-Spoke Atlas Networking"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:e3680c5008b3f183560e1f34df5d82321c8b997f9c27e438f231d1642547cf2e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:50a6ac47252878f76667730ba8d739e497cc87ba372f40ea67d251989ddc81de", "ev:a468486683e0ca6cae1434eb3801728f3006dfe07f955d9fcab3aeabaa48fc56"]}
{"id": "clm:63fa5b9b87d70665086b83c918fe4fde4396f9e2bbda560ae6f9ca6dd561f8a5", "type": "statement", "text": "For Atlas VNet peering on Azure, use the Private IP for Peering connection string, allow the peer CIDR in Atlas, and configure cloud-side routing. The standard Azure connection string must not be assumed to select the private peering path. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/security-vpc-peering/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Hub-and-Spoke Atlas Networking"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:e3680c5008b3f183560e1f34df5d82321c8b997f9c27e438f231d1642547cf2e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:ff5d0316bbdec06a091a64dd05d2e14c538dcbd1f8058a06e96c0da81ac3025c"]}
{"id": "clm:53ca8c898fac2d4e03e82621ce3773b23f73e56306d354c03c80e067b562e1c8", "type": "statement", "text": "An Atlas private endpoint in a hub VNet can serve clients in directly peered spoke VNets and an ExpressRoute-connected on-premises network. MongoDB explicitly supports these access paths; this does not make ordinary VNet peering transitive. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/security-private-endpoint.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Hub-and-Spoke Atlas Networking"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/architecture/networking/guide/private-link-hub-spoke-network", "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/architecture/reference-architectures/hybrid-networking/virtual-network-peering"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:e3680c5008b3f183560e1f34df5d82321c8b997f9c27e438f231d1642547cf2e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:38aebd940e8856ba88aa47aa555c39d44ef57c314e84e5098701c29307261c4e", "ev:6ec20238313b220d3643cff0efe4e5159e231be933d217e11309a4426750c324"]}
{"id": "clm:e47568ee1fc9ffe8ee2d97537bd30a094c13701213e246817619f70d3ffcb0cf", "type": "statement", "text": "A default route of 0.0.0.0/0 to the hub firewall does not override a private endpoint route. Enable route-table network policies on the endpoint subnet and configure an eligible, sufficiently specific UDR to steer requests through inspection. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/architecture/networking/guide/private-link-hub-spoke-network", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Hub-and-Spoke Atlas Networking"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/private-link/disable-private-endpoint-network-policy"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:e3680c5008b3f183560e1f34df5d82321c8b997f9c27e438f231d1642547cf2e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:ce5b953a7df66512f945a4189a0b3f7665d724099a5eb1b545e5c4d4468b10cd"]}
{"id": "clm:dc0915781ecf504ecf372a9b63959139e7ff0e045ca9c5b058cc62ba1f957684", "type": "statement", "text": "Endpoint-subnet NSG enforcement requires private-endpoint network policies for NSGs. Merely putting an NSG on the subnet does not establish that its rules filter private-endpoint traffic. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/architecture/networking/guide/private-link-hub-spoke-network", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Hub-and-Spoke Atlas Networking"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/private-link/disable-private-endpoint-network-policy"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:e3680c5008b3f183560e1f34df5d82321c8b997f9c27e438f231d1642547cf2e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:97ece722e9285b6c78a05c0311750438c4033b1f214db9844b72c5dfade7863a"]}
{"id": "clm:5eae96d6b823e2a24d677c1d55961b201091ad87a19c15698aac535ebee18fb2", "type": "statement", "text": "For a peering-based Atlas design, plan non-overlapping CIDRs, allow the peer CIDR in Atlas, and configure cloud-side routing. These are separate requirements from connecting application spokes to a shared private endpoint. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/security-vpc-peering.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Hub-and-Spoke Atlas Networking"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:e3680c5008b3f183560e1f34df5d82321c8b997f9c27e438f231d1642547cf2e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:96183d9242d0f21a833f6d6b5598fd68b8dba9d16086e56f4e156de67e44c8ca", "ev:bd70da1599665849dcb535805aa9900cb1a57b79750ed199c6f4cb81cbc69779"]}
{"id": "clm:9af35c413802f58a209e5693806ff6496d821c9301bd2dc1bd9862ca2d09f177", "type": "statement", "text": "Palo Alto Networks documents Virtual WAN private-traffic routing intent for inspection of spoke-to-spoke VM flows through Cloud NGFW. Its documented absence of east-west SNAT concerns VM examples; it does not establish that an Atlas private endpoint needs no SNAT. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://docs.paloaltonetworks.com/cloud-ngfw-azure/deployment/cloud-ngfw-for-azure-deployment-architectures/cloud-ngfw-for-azure-virtual-wan", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Hub-and-Spoke Atlas Networking"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:e3680c5008b3f183560e1f34df5d82321c8b997f9c27e438f231d1642547cf2e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:f4ed8c0faf1c842eddd1c37a304961a01d5048c5523f21570c26c13e686b5936"]}
{"id": "clm:905cb2f82b57ebd7b89ce9d16a5bce10923b929330227510367f958ffd5f1198", "type": "statement", "text": "Microsoft documents /32 private-endpoint routes that propagate across configured VNet peerings. A first-hand Azure hub-and-spoke report describes a Storage private-endpoint return path bypassing the hub firewall, and commenters discuss asymmetric inspection and SNAT. Use this as general Azure troubleshooting evidence; it does not establish Atlas-specific behavior or universal cross-spoke connectivity. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/architecture/networking/guide/private-link-hub-spoke-network", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Hub-and-Spoke Atlas Networking"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://nicolgit.github.io/cross-spokes-routing-for-private-endpoint/", "https://www.reddit.com/r/AZURE/comments/1n7eoq6/azure_private_endpoints_unexpected_routing_in/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:e3680c5008b3f183560e1f34df5d82321c8b997f9c27e438f231d1642547cf2e", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:44fdcdd720f4807a24ae831f2ac6ee34ea81be00d722fcf787fdd775bb99234b", "ev:6be1ffe826528aa8a2aaf6828367a82767c1aa192f8bdc465adb6f9904bb7759", "ev:d3b993061f02601870c048823f4f19efaf815b1c4f779e298065bc55872b2b0e"]}
